WEBVTT

1
-1:59:59,990 --> 00:00:07.328
Cognitive radios hunt for free channels across a wide band, and deep networks find them well from raw I/Q samples.

2
00:00:06.913 --> 00:00:14.436
But stored as thirty-two-bit floats, these networks are too heavy for the small, low-power devices many radios run on.

3
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.245
The paper trains them with quantization-aware training.

4
00:00:17.941 --> 00:00:23.944
Weights and activations become eight-bit integers, and the network learns to tolerate the rounding.

5
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:31.205
With windows of one hundred twenty-eight samples, every quantized model keeps an F1-score above zero point nine eight.

6
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.990
On a Sony Spresense microcontroller, every quantized model is smaller and faster.

7
00:00:36.686 --> 00:00:42.456
One shrinks by seventy-two percent, and another cuts its inference time by fifty-one percent.

8
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:48.398
Far smaller and faster spectrum sensing, at nearly the same F1-score when the window is long enough.
